## Release vm.args — extends the default mix release template with Erlang
## distribution bound to loopback (research.md §R11/§R12), so the node is
## reachable only via `docker exec ... bin/speckit_orchestrator remote`
## (FR-025), never over the container's network interface.
##
## Deliberately does NOT set -sname/-setcookie here: those come from
## `bin/RELEASE_NAME`'s own `--cookie "$RELEASE_COOKIE"` /
## `$(release_distribution "$RELEASE_NODE")` flags, which are genuine shell
## substitution and always correct. A `${RELEASE_COOKIE}`-style token written
## directly in this file is NOT substituted at boot — proven live: it reaches
## erl as the *literal* string "${RELEASE_COOKIE}", silently overriding the
## correct `-setcookie` already set by the flags above (args are order-applied,
## last wins) and rejecting every real distributed connection with "Invalid
## challenge reply" (an apparent cookie mismatch, cookie strings verified
## byte-identical between processes — the actual mismatch is this file's own
## unexpanded placeholder against the real generated cookie).
##
## (No explicit -mode here: the release runner script already passes
## `--erl "-mode $RELEASE_MODE"` unconditionally, so one here would just be a
## harmless-but-noisy duplicate.)

-kernel inet_dist_use_interface '{127,0,0,1}'
